Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:46:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] throttler: Bump global pending connection limit to 1000

Before we had 5 as the limit per peer, and 10 global. That meant 2 peers
could easily cause any other peer to fail to connect. Change the limit
to 1000, meaning one need at least 200.

Part-of: <https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-remote-desktop/-/merge_requests/436>
(cherry picked from commit cf336009550240b369df99c165540f2fa46494fe)
(cherry picked from commit 0dde187d6fdf6a014f1cc619e700ff1cf40a0d6b)
---
 src/grd-throttler.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/grd-throttler.c b/src/grd-throttler.c
index 1f8985a..fdab7d9 100644
--- a/src/grd-throttler.c
+++ b/src/grd-throttler.c
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@
 
 #define DEFAULT_MAX_CONNECTIONS_PER_PEER 5
 #define DEFAULT_MAX_PENDING_CONNECTIONS 5
-#define DEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS_PER_SECOND 10
+#define DEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS_PER_SECOND 1000
 
 struct _GrdThrottlerLimits
 {
-- 
2.53.0

